# Doing two things at once in Russian: читая, прочитав
subtitle: "Masha's letter after a weekend in Petersburg: learn to read Russian gerunds — читая (while reading) and прочитав (having read)."
tags: ["russian","russian gerunds","читая","reading russian","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/gerunds","grammar/narrative-words"]
thumb: "band \"Two things at once in Russian\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"If only in Russian: если бы","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/128-russian-if-only.cast"}

## Doing two things at once in Russian: читая, прочитав
stress: new
level: basic
